// The object carries its module list (KG Gap obj_lane_module_dependency,
// decided 2026-09-07): `import m;` binds libm at parse, and the .o this
// unit compiles to records libm's TARGET spelling in __madc_module_deps, so
// the single-object lane opens it before load — no -l on the command line.
// libm's symbols happen to be reachable in madc's own process, so the JIT
// and exe lanes never needed the table; the gate script asserts the table
// itself in the emitted C11 (scripts/check-object-module-deps.sh), and the
// GUI stage's .o lane (import madcwebview — a library madc does NOT link)
// is where the mechanism carries real weight. (madc dialect: `import` is
// a directive there as in C++20, and the intrinsics need no include.)
import m;

int main()
{
    println("sqrt {}", (int)sqrt(16.0));
    println("cbrt {}", (int)cbrt(27.0));
    return 0;
}
